window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-71636f336b61afaa"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"run-code-migrations\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">执行代码迁移</h1> <p>按受控检查点迁移旧技术栈。</p> <p>使用 Codex 将旧系统映射到新技术栈，分里程碑完成迁移，并在每次切换前验证行为是否一致。</p> <p><a id=\"best-for\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">适合哪些情况</h2> <ul> <li>从旧技术栈迁移到现代技术栈，需要更换框架、运行时、构建系统或平台惯例的项目。</li> <li>需要兼容层、分阶段切换，并在每个迁移检查点进行明确验证的团队。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"skills-plugins\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">技能与插件</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>技能或插件</th> <th>用途</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/skills/tree/main/skills/.curated/security-best-practices\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">$security-best-practices（需联网）</a></td> <td>合并前检查高风险迁移、依赖变化和对外暴露的接口与功能。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/skills/tree/main/skills/.curated/gh-fix-ci\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">$gh-fix-ci（需联网）</a></td> <td>每个迁移里程碑后及时处理失败的 CI 检查，不要把修复工作都留到最后。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/skills/tree/main/skills/.curated/aspnet-core\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">$aspnet-core（需联网）</a></td> <td>当迁移涉及 ASP.NET Core 应用模型、<code>Program.cs</code>、中间件、测试、性能或版本升级时，使用对应框架的指导。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"starter-prompt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">起步提示词</h2> <p>在约束下迁移</p> <p>建议模型：<code>gpt-6-astra</code> · 建议推理级别：<code>medium</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">将这个代码库从 [legacy stack or system] 迁移到 [target stack or system]。\n\n要求：\n- 先盘点旧系统的前提与约定：路由、数据模型、身份验证、配置、构建工具、测试、部署和外部契约。\n- 将旧技术栈映射到新技术栈，并指出没有直接对应项的内容。\n- 提出带有兼容层或检查点的增量迁移计划，不要一次性大规模重写。\n- 除非迁移明确要求对用户可见的变化，否则保持行为不变。\n- 分里程碑开展工作，每个里程碑后运行 lint、类型检查和有针对性的测试。\n- 在切换完成前，始终明确保留回滚或备用方案。\n- 验证失败时，先修复再继续。\n- 先梳理迁移涉及的范围，并提出检查点计划。\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"related-links\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">关联文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/cookbook/examples/codex/code_modernization\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">使用 Codex 现代化改造代码库（需联网）</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/codex/use-cases/follow-goals\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">持续推进目标（需联网）</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-d955137d94c4d306\">ChatGPT 桌面应用中的工作树</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"introduction\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">简介</h2> <p>从一种技术栈迁移到另一种时，可以借助 Codex 规划并执行受控迁移。涉及的内容包括路由、数据模型、配置、身份验证、后台作业、构建工具、部署、测试，甚至语言和框架本身的惯例。</p> <p>Codex 适合这类工作，因为它能够盘点旧系统、将旧概念映射到新概念，并按检查点逐步完成变化，而不是进行一次巨大的重写。当你需要淘汰旧框架、移植到新运行时，或在产品必须保持可用的同时逐步替换技术栈时，这一点尤为重要。</p> <p><a id=\"how-to-use\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">如何使用</h2> <ol> <li>先盘点迁移涉及的范围：旧软件包、框架惯例、路由、数据访问、身份验证、配置、构建工具、测试、部署前提，以及迁移后必须保持兼容的外部契约。</li> <li>让 Codex 将旧概念映射到目标技术栈，并指出没有直接对应项的内容。</li> <li>选择增量策略：兼容层、逐模块移植、通过抽象层分支切换，或围绕单个边界逐步替换的绞杀者式迁移。</li> <li>在迁移本身要求可见变化之前，保持行为稳定；对于这些例外，要明确说明。</li> <li>每个里程碑后，运行能证明行为一致性的最小验证集：lint、类型检查、有针对性的测试、契约测试、冒烟测试，或与旧实现路径进行并排对照。</li> <li>每个检查点后都审查差异和剩余的切换风险，不要等到整个重写完成后再检查。</li> </ol> <p><a id=\"leverage-execplans\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"execplans\">借助 ExecPlans</h2> <p>在<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/cookbook/examples/codex/code_modernization.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">代码现代化改造 Cookbook</a> 中，我们介绍了 ExecPlans：这类文档可以让 Codex 总览清理工作、明确预期的最终状态，并记录每轮完成后的验证结果。 让 Codex 执行复杂迁移时，可以要求它为系统的每个部分创建一份 ExecPlan，确保每项决定和技术栈选择都有记录，便于日后审查。</p> <p><a id=\"combine-with-a-goal\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_8\">与目标结合</h2> <p>对于耗时较长的迁移工作片段，可以使用<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/use-cases/follow-goals\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">目标（本地尚未收录）</a>引导 Codex 持续推进。设定目标时，明确最终状态、行为一致性检查、回滚要求和停止条件。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"run-code-migrations\">Run code migrations</h1> <p>Migrate legacy stacks in controlled checkpoints.</p> <p>Use Codex to map a legacy system to a new stack, land the move in milestones, and validate parity before each transition.</p> <h2 id=\"best-for\">Best for</h2> <ul> <li>Legacy-to-modern stack moves where frameworks, runtimes, build systems, or platform conventions need to change.</li> <li>Teams that need compatibility layers, phased transitions, and explicit validation at each migration checkpoint.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"skills-plugins\">Skills &amp; Plugins</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Skill or plugin</th> <th>Why use it</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/skills/tree/main/skills/.curated/security-best-practices\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">$security-best-practices (online)</a></td> <td>Check risky migrations, dependency changes, and exposed surfaces before you merge.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/skills/tree/main/skills/.curated/gh-fix-ci\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">$gh-fix-ci (online)</a></td> <td>Work through failing CI after each migration milestone instead of leaving cleanup until the end.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/skills/tree/main/skills/.curated/aspnet-core\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">$aspnet-core (online)</a></td> <td>Use framework-specific guidance when a migration touches ASP.NET Core app models, <code>Program.cs</code>, middleware, testing, performance, or version upgrades.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"starter-prompt\">Starter prompt</h2> <p>Migrate With Guardrails</p> <p>Suggested model：<code>gpt-6-astra</code> · Suggested reasoning effort：<code>medium</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Migrate this codebase from [legacy stack or system] to [target stack or system].\n\nRequirements:\n- Start by inventorying the legacy assumptions: routing, data models, auth, configuration, build tooling, tests, deployment, and external contracts.\n- Map the old stack to the new one and call out anything that has no direct equivalent.\n- Propose an incremental migration plan with compatibility layers or checkpoints instead of one big rewrite.\n- Keep behavior unchanged unless the migration explicitly requires a user-visible change.\n- Work in milestones and run lint, type-check, and focused tests after each milestone.\n- Keep rollback or fallback options visible until the transition is complete.\n- If validation fails, fix it before continuing.\n- Start by mapping the migration surface and proposing the checkpoint plan.\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"related-links\">Related links</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/cookbook/examples/codex/code_modernization\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Modernizing your Codebase with Codex (online)</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/codex/use-cases/follow-goals\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Follow a goal (online)</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-d955137d94c4d306\">Worktrees in the ChatGPT desktop app</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"introduction\">Introduction</h2> <p>When you are moving from one stack to another, you can leverage Codex to map and execute a controlled migration: routing, data models, configuration, auth, background jobs, build tooling, deployment, tests, or even the language and framework conventions themselves.</p> <p>Codex is useful here because it can inventory the legacy system, map old concepts to new ones, and land the change in checkpoints instead of one giant rewrite. That matters when you are moving off a legacy framework, porting to a new runtime, or incrementally replacing one stack with another while the product still has to keep working.</p> <h2 id=\"how-to-use\">How to use</h2> <ol> <li>Start by inventorying the migration surface: legacy packages, framework conventions, routing, data access, auth, configuration, build tooling, tests, deployment assumptions, and any external contracts that must survive the move.</li> <li>Ask Codex to map the legacy concepts to the target stack and call out what has no direct match.</li> <li>Choose an incremental strategy: compatibility layer, module-by-module port, branch-by-abstraction, or a strangler-style replacement around one boundary at a time.</li> <li>Keep behavior stable until the migration itself forces a visible change, and name those exceptions explicitly.</li> <li>After each milestone, run the smallest validation that proves parity: lint, type-check, focused tests, contract tests, smoke tests, or a side-by-side check against the legacy path.</li> <li>Review the diff and the remaining transition risk after each checkpoint instead of waiting for the full rewrite.</li> </ol> <h2 id=\"leverage-execplans\">Leverage ExecPlans</h2> <p>In our <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/cookbook/examples/codex/code_modernization.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">code modernization cookbook</a>, we introduce ExecPlans: documents that let Codex keep an overview of the cleanup, spell out the intended end state, and log validation after each pass. When you ask Codex to run a complex migration, ask it to create an ExecPlan for each part of the system to make sure every decision and tech stack choice is recorded and can be reviewed later.</p> <h2 id=\"combine-with-a-goal\">Combine with a goal</h2> <p>For long-running migration slices, use a <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/use-cases/follow-goals\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">goal (not in this local snapshot)</a> to guide Codex through the work. Set the goal with a clear end state, parity checks, rollback expectations, and a stopping condition.</p>"};
